<title>KUWAIT: Kuwaiti bank assets slip in September.</title>
<headline>Kuwaiti bank assets slip in September.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of Kuwaiti banks fell to 11.134 billion dinars at the end of September from 11.144 billion at the end of August, the Central Bank's monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.378 billion dinars in September 1995.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					   September '96    September '95</p>
<p> Cash					  43.8		 48.7</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	    19.7		  3.2</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	     1825.1	     1986.3</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		   2907.6	     3713.3</p>
<p> Other local investments		305.0		306.1</p>
<p> Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents				3008.9	     2161.1</p>
<p> Foreign assets			  2041.3	     2115.8</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    527.9		576.1</p>
<p> Other assets			     455.0		467.9</p>
<p> Total				    11134.4	    11378.4</p>
<p>Note. Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.2988 dinars)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom +965-243-1920</p>
</text>
